+# G2 stage polish2: the visual critic's second pass, worked most visible first
+
+Stage agent polish2, branch `g2/polish2` (cut from `g2/trunk` f86ebf7, polish1 integrated), 2026-11-12. Scope: the
+thirteen ranked issues of the visual critic's iteration 2 on the benchmark scenes A–E, as many as could be done well,
+then the canonical capture set again and before/after sheets per issue. MonoGame 3D only, presentation only (DR42:
+nothing here reads back into the simulation; the battle trace of scenes C and D is read-only, and the tests that read it
+hash it before and after). All numbers below were measured in this container on **llvmpipe (Mesa software GL on 4
+logical CPUs of an Intel Xeon at 2.10 GHz, 15 GB RAM, shared with other sessions): llvmpipe, not Victus evidence**. No
+hardware GPU ran this code. The Director's quality references were used as references only; nothing player-facing names
+another game (D-069). These are prototype frames, not production art.
+
+**Verdict, honestly.** @@VERDICT@@
+
+## 1. What changed, per issue
+
+Before = polish1's canonical captures (`captures/polish1/`, G2 at polish1's final build); after = this stage's canonical
+captures (`captures/polish2/`, §2), both 1920 × 1080 with 8 samples. The measured figures come from
+`scripts/measure-polish2.py BEFORE AFTER` (committed: mean colour, its HSV hue and saturation, local contrast as the
+median luminance standard deviation in 24 px windows, the share of near-white pixels, and the saturation of the
+brightest tenth of a region) or from the tests of §3. Each row's sheet is `captures/polish2/sheets/polish2-NN-*.jpg`
+(before left, after right).
